---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../../components/Footer.astro';

const steps = [
  {
    number: '01',
    title: 'Anesthesia',
    body: 'Local anesthesia is administered to the tooth and surrounding tissues. We use buffered anesthesia and fine-gauge needles to minimize discomfort at injection. The tooth and surrounding area become fully numb before any instrumentation begins. Patients who are anxious about achieving profound anesthesia should know that supplemental techniques — intraligamentary injection, intrapulpal delivery — are available for teeth that are more difficult to numb.',
  },
  {
    number: '02',
    title: 'Access',
    body: 'A small opening is made through the crown of the tooth under operating microscope magnification. The pulp chamber is entered, and the canals are identified. The microscope allows identification of all canal orifices, including accessory canals and calcified entrances that would be invisible to the naked eye.',
  },
  {
    number: '03',
    title: 'Instrumentation',
    body: 'Nickel-titanium rotary files are used to shape and clean the canal system. Working length — the precise depth to the root tip — is confirmed with an electronic apex locator and radiographic verification. Irrigation with sodium hypochlorite and EDTA solution dissolves pulp remnants and disrupts bacterial biofilm throughout the canal.',
  },
  {
    number: '04',
    title: 'Obturation',
    body: 'Once the canals are cleaned, shaped, and dried, they are filled with warm gutta-percha and a biocompatible sealer. The three-dimensional fill of the canal system creates a hermetic seal that prevents recontamination. A temporary or definitive coronal seal is placed at the end of the appointment.',
  },
  {
    number: '05',
    title: 'Restoration',
    body: 'Root canal treatment is not complete until the tooth is fully restored by your general dentist — typically with a crown within 4–6 weeks. We send a detailed treatment report to your referring dentist. The crown protects the treated tooth from fracture, which is the most common reason a successfully treated tooth is eventually lost.',
  },
];

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'Does a root canal hurt?',
    a: 'No — a root canal relieves pain rather than causing it. The procedure is performed under local anesthesia, and most patients describe feeling pressure but no pain during treatment. Post-treatment soreness for 1–3 days is managed with over-the-counter analgesics in most cases. Patients are frequently surprised by how comfortable the experience is.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How long does root canal treatment take?',
    a: 'A single-rooted tooth — a front tooth or a premolar with straightforward anatomy — can often be completed in 60–90 minutes. Multi-rooted teeth (molars), calcified canals, or cases with complex anatomy may require 90–120 minutes or a second appointment. We give you a realistic time estimate at your consultation.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is the success rate for root canal treatment?',
    a: 'Published long-term studies consistently show success rates above 90% for root canal treatment performed under modern conditions — microscopic magnification, precise instrumentation, and a definitive coronal restoration. Cases involving larger periapical lesions may take longer to heal radiographically but generally achieve similar long-term outcomes.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do I still need a crown after a root canal?',
    a: 'In most cases, yes. The access cavity and the absence of vital pulp tissue make the tooth more susceptible to fracture. A crown placed by your general dentist seals the tooth and distributes bite forces to protect it. Front teeth with minimal structure loss sometimes do not require a crown, but your dentist will advise based on the specific situation.',
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Root Canal Treatment in Laguna Hills, CA — Saddleback Valley Endodontics"
  description="Root canal treatment in Laguna Hills and Mission Viejo, CA. Board-certified endodontists, operating microscope, same-day urgent appointments. (949) 837-3033."
>
  <Header variant="solid" />

  <main>

    <section class="page-intro">
      <p class="page-eyebrow">Root Canal Treatment · Laguna Hills, CA</p>
      <h1 class="page-title">Root canal treatment.</h1>
      <p class="page-lede">
        Modern root canal therapy is nothing like the procedure's reputation suggests.
        Performed under microscope by a fellowship-trained endodontist, it is a precise,
        comfortable treatment that saves teeth and relieves pain.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="rct-intro-section">
      <div class="rct-intro-inner">
        <div class="rct-intro-body">
          <h2 class="rct-section-headline">What is root canal treatment?</h2>
          <p>Root canal treatment — formally, endodontic therapy — removes infected or inflamed pulp tissue from the interior of a tooth, cleans and shapes the canal system, and seals it to prevent reinfection. The term "root canal" refers to the natural cavity within the root of a tooth; endodontic therapy addresses what happens inside that space.</p>
          <p>The pulp is the soft tissue at the center of the tooth containing nerves, blood vessels, and connective tissue. Once a tooth is fully formed, the pulp is not essential to the tooth's function — a tooth can survive without it, nourished by the surrounding tissues. Root canal treatment preserves the outer structure of the tooth while eliminating the source of infection.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rct-when-block">
          <h2 class="rct-when-title">When is it needed?</h2>
          <ul class="rct-when-list">
            <li>Irreversible pulpitis — inflammation that will not resolve on its own</li>
            <li>Pulp necrosis — pulp tissue that has died due to infection or trauma</li>
            <li>Apical periodontitis — infection spread to the bone at the root tip</li>
            <li>Dental abscess — acute localized infection with or without swelling</li>
            <li>Deep decay extending into the pulp</li>
            <li>Severe fracture exposing the pulp</li>
            <li>Traumatic injury with pulp involvement</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="rct-steps-section">
      <div class="rct-steps-header">
        <p class="rct-steps-eyebrow">The Procedure</p>
        <h2 class="rct-steps-headline">Step by step.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="rct-steps">
        {steps.map(s => (
          <div class="rct-step">
            <div class="rct-step-number">{s.number}</div>
            <div class="rct-step-content">
              <h3 class="rct-step-title">{s.title}</h3>
              <p class="rct-step-body">{s.body}</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="rct-recovery-section">
      <div class="rct-recovery-inner">
        <p class="rct-recovery-eyebrow">Recovery</p>
        <h2 class="rct-recovery-headline">What to expect afterward.</h2>
        <p class="rct-recovery-body">
          Most patients return to normal activity the same day or the following day. Mild
          soreness and sensitivity on the treated tooth for 1–3 days is normal and expected.
          Over-the-counter ibuprofen is sufficient for most patients. Avoid chewing hard food
          on the treated side until the permanent crown is placed. Full post-operative
          instructions are provided at your appointment and available on our{' '}
          <a href="/post-operative-instructions/">post-op care page</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="rct-faq-section">
      <div class="rct-faq-header">
        <p class="rct-faq-eyebrow">Common Questions</p>
        <h2 class="rct-faq-headline">Root canal FAQ.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="rct-faq-list">
        {faqs.map(f => (
          <details class="rct-faq-item" name="rct-faq">
            <summary class="rct-faq-q">
              <span>{f.q}</span>
              <span class="rct-faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </summary>
            <div class="rct-faq-a">
              <p>{f.a}</p>
            </div>
          </details>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="rct-cta-band">
      <div class="rct-cta-inner">
        <p class="rct-cta-eyebrow">Serving Laguna Hills & Mission Viejo</p>
        <h2 class="rct-cta-headline">Same-day appointments for urgent tooth pain.</h2>
        <p class="rct-cta-body">
          Call <a href="tel:+19498373033">(949) 837-3033</a> or request online. We are at
          25800 Jeronimo Road, Suite 300, Mission Viejo — minutes from Laguna Hills.
        </p>
        <a href="/request-an-appointment/" class="rct-cta-btn">Request an Appointment</a>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style is:global>
  main { padding-top: var(--header-h); }

  .page-intro {
    padding: clamp(80px, 13vh, 140px) clamp(28px, 6vw, 88px) clamp(60px, 9vh, 100px);
    max-width: 960px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line);
  }
  .page-eyebrow {
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.36em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
    margin: 0 0 32px;
  }
  .page-title {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: clamp(52px, 8vw, 104px);
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    margin: 0 0 28px;
  }
  .page-lede {
    font-size: clamp(16px, 1.5vw, 19px);
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
    max-width: 58ch;
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* Intro */
  .rct-intro-section {
    padding: clamp(80px, 12vh, 140px) clamp(28px, 6vw, 88px);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line);
  }
  .rct-intro-inner {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 420px;
    gap: clamp(48px, 7vw, 88px);
    align-items: start;
    max-width: 1200px;
  }
  .rct-section-headline {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: clamp(26px, 3.2vw, 40px);
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.008em;
    margin: 0 0 24px;
  }
  .rct-intro-body p {
    font-size: clamp(15px, 1.3vw, 17px);
    line-height: 1.72;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
    margin: 0 0 18px;
  }
  .rct-when-block {
    background: var(--color-paper-warm);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    padding: clamp(28px, 4vw, 44px);
  }
  .rct-when-title {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(18px, 2vw, 24px);
    line-height: 1.2;
    margin: 0 0 20px;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  .rct-when-list {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }
  .rct-when-list li {
    font-size: clamp(13px, 1.1vw, 15px);
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
    padding: 10px 0 10px 18px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    position: relative;
  }
  .rct-when-list li:first-child { border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line); }
  .rct-when-list li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 50%;
    width: 7px;
    height: 1px;
    background: var(--color-ink-soft);
    opacity: 0.5;
  }

  /* Steps */
  .rct-steps-section {
    padding: clamp(80px, 12vh, 140px) clamp(28px, 6vw, 88px);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line);
  }
  .rct-steps-header { margin-bottom: clamp(48px, 7vh, 72px); }
  .rct-steps-eyebrow {
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.36em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
    margin: 0 0 20px;
  }
  .rct-steps-headline {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: clamp(28px, 4vw, 52px);
    line-height: 1.05;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .rct-steps { max-width: 840px; }
  .rct-step {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 72px 1fr;
    gap: 0 clamp(24px, 4vw, 52px);
    padding: clamp(40px, 6vh, 64px) 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line);
  }
  .rct-step:first-child { border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line); }
  .rct-step-number {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(30px, 3.2vw, 44px);
    font-weight: 300;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
    opacity: 0.35;
    line-height: 1.1;
    padding-top: 4px;
  }
  .rct-step-title {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(20px, 2.2vw, 28px);
    line-height: 1.15;
    letter-spacing: -0.005em;
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  .rct-step-body {
    font-size: clamp(15px, 1.3vw, 17px);
    line-height: 1.72;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 62ch;
  }

  /* Recovery */
  .rct-recovery-section {
    background: var(--color-paper-warm);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    padding: clamp(80px, 12vh, 140px) clamp(28px, 6vw, 88px);
  }
  .rct-recovery-inner { max-width: 720px; }
  .rct-recovery-eyebrow {
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.36em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
    margin: 0 0 20px;
  }
  .rct-recovery-headline {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: clamp(28px, 4vw, 48px);
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.008em;
    margin: 0 0 20px;
  }
  .rct-recovery-body {
    font-size: clamp(15px, 1.3vw, 17px);
    line-height: 1.72;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .rct-recovery-body a { border-bottom: 1px solid currentColor; transition: opacity 0.2s; }
  .rct-recovery-body a:hover { opacity: 0.6; }

  /* FAQ */
  .rct-faq-section {
    padding: clamp(80px, 12vh, 140px) clamp(28px, 6vw, 88px);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line);
  }
  .rct-faq-header { margin-bottom: clamp(40px, 6vh, 60px); }
  .rct-faq-eyebrow {
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.36em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
    margin: 0 0 20px;
  }
  .rct-faq-headline {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: clamp(28px, 4vw, 52px);
    line-height: 1.05;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .rct-faq-list { max-width: 840px; }
  .rct-faq-item { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line); }
  .rct-faq-item:first-child { border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line); }
  .rct-faq-q {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 24px;
    padding: clamp(20px, 3vh, 30px) 0;
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(18px, 2vw, 26px);
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.2;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    transition: color 0.2s var(--ease-out);
  }
  .rct-faq-q::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
  .rct-faq-q:hover { color: var(--color-ink-soft); }
  .rct-faq-icon {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 20px;
    height: 20px;
    position: relative;
  }
  .rct-faq-icon::before,
  .rct-faq-icon::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    background: currentColor;
    transition: transform 0.3s var(--ease-out), opacity 0.25s var(--ease-out);
  }
  .rct-faq-icon::before { width: 1px; height: 100%; left: 50%; top: 0; transform: translateX(-50%); }
  .rct-faq-icon::after  { width: 100%; height: 1px; top: 50%; left: 0; transform: translateY(-50%); }
  .rct-faq-item[open] .rct-faq-icon::before { transform: translateX(-50%) rotate(90deg); opacity: 0; }
  .rct-faq-a {
    padding: 0 0 clamp(20px, 3.5vh, 32px);
    max-width: 66ch;
  }
  .rct-faq-a p {
    font-size: clamp(15px, 1.3vw, 17px);
    line-height: 1.72;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* CTA */
  .rct-cta-band {
    padding: clamp(80px, 12vh, 140px) clamp(28px, 6vw, 88px);
  }
  .rct-cta-inner { max-width: 640px; }
  .rct-cta-eyebrow {
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.36em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
    margin: 0 0 28px;
  }
  .rct-cta-headline {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: clamp(28px, 4vw, 48px);
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.008em;
    margin: 0 0 20px;
  }
  .rct-cta-body {
    font-size: clamp(15px, 1.3vw, 17px);
    line-height: 1.68;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
    margin: 0 0 36px;
  }
  .rct-cta-body a { border-bottom: 1px solid currentColor; transition: opacity 0.2s; }
  .rct-cta-body a:hover { opacity: 0.6; }
  .rct-cta-btn {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.28em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-weight: 500;
    padding: 16px 36px;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-ink);
    color: var(--color-ink);
    transition: background 0.28s var(--ease-out), color 0.28s var(--ease-out);
  }
  .rct-cta-btn:hover {
    background: var(--color-ink);
    color: var(--color-paper);
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .rct-intro-inner { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .rct-step { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 8px 0; }
    .rct-step-number { font-size: 28px; }
  }
</style>
